.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH mnnn-code-create 1  "mnnn-code-create 2.16.1" 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
mnnn\-code\-create \- Create a code space (not approved to run yet)
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmnnn code create\fR [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-\-lang\fR] [\fB\-\-db\fR] [\fB\-\-from\fR] [\fB\-f\fR|\fB\-\-file\fR] [\fB\-\-non\-interactive\fR] [\fB\-\-source\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-\-editor\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-input\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-model\fR] [\fB\-\-theme\-mode\fR] [\fB\-\-where\fR] [\fB\-\-matching\fR] [\fB\-\-group\fR] [\fB\-\-sort\fR] [\fB\-\-limit\fR] [\fB\-\-description\fR] [\fB\-\-project\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fINAME\fR> 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create a code space (not approved to run yet)
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Muninn home directory (default ~/.muninn)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_HOME\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-lang\fR \fI<LANG>\fR

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
math
.IP \(bu 2
polars
.IP \(bu 2
rust
.IP \(bu 2
python
.IP \(bu 2
plugin: A prebuilt plugin (the source is the path of the library)
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-db\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Database file (default <home>/storage/muninn.database)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_DB\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-from\fR \fI<FROM>\fR
Start from a copy of a code space or a built\-in parser (`mnnn code parsers`)
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-file\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Read the source from a file (`\-` reads standard input)
.TP
\fB\-\-non\-interactive\fR
Never prompt; missing values are errors
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_NON_INTERACTIVE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-source\fR \fI<SOURCE>\fR
The source itself
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
More output (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-editor\fR
Write the source in $VISUAL or $EDITOR
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Print nothing but errors and requested data
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_QUIET\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-input\fR \fI<INPUT>\fR
Default input from another source: `search:NAME` (any live search), `journal:NAME`, `code:SPACE` (its output) or a model query (`bars where … limit N`). A convenience: whatever is piped in (`mnnn pipe`, share) is what a run works on
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Answer yes to every confirmation
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_YES\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-model\fR \fI<MODEL>\fR
Model to read (`bars` or a designed model)
.TP
\fB\-\-theme\-mode\fR \fI<THEME_MODE>\fR
Override the theme mode for this run
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
light
.IP \(bu 2
dark
.IP \(bu 2
system
.RE
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_THEME_MODE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-where\fR \fI<FILTER>\fR
Condition FIELD OP VALUE (repeatable; `;` separates several)
.TP
\fB\-\-matching\fR \fI<MATCHING>\fR
Records whose text fields contain this
.TP
\fB\-\-group\fR \fI<GROUP>\fR
Group by these fields (math computes per group; repeatable or comma\-separated)
.TP
\fB\-\-sort\fR \fI<SORT>\fR
Sort by these fields (`\-F` descending; repeatable or comma\-separated)
.TP
\fB\-\-limit\fR \fI<LIMIT>\fR
At most this many records
.TP
\fB\-\-description\fR \fI<DESCRIPTION>\fR [default: ]

.TP
\fB\-\-project\fR \fI<PROJECT>\fR
Add it to a project
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fINAME\fR>

.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH VERSION
v2.16.1
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBmnnn\fR(1)
